</td><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7cccc191-abaf-8098-ccf3-e04764f67345" id="_7cccc191-abaf-8098-ccf3-e04764f67345"></a><b>Mandatory in S-102</b><br/> A single value may be provided when all axes have a common resolution. <br/> For multiple value provision, use axis order as specified in dataset. <br/> For example, for 5 metre resolution, the value 5 must be encoded. <br/> If the grid cell size varies over the extent of the grid <br/> (i.e., when using a geographic grid), an approximated value should be used.</p>
</td></tr></tbody><tfoot><tr><td colspan="6" style="border-top:0pt;mso-border-top-alt:0pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;"><div class="Note"><a name="note-s100datacoverage-boundingPolygon" id="note-s100datacoverage-boundingPolygon"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span><i>boundingPolygon</i> is restricted to a single GML Polygon with one exterior and 0 or more interiors expressed as Linear Rings using SRS EPSG:4326. The exterior and optional interiors shall be composed of a closed sequence of &gt;=4 coordinate positions expressed individually or as a list (posList). The GML polygon shall have a valid GML identifier.</p></div></td></tr></tfoot></table></div>


</div>

<div><a name="_s100_purpose" id="_s100_purpose"></a><h3>12.5.3<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>S100_Purpose</h3>

